{"name":"White Bean Hummus","hex":"#e8d0b2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"},{"term":"bean","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant of several genera of the taxonomic family Fabaceae that produces large edible seeds or edible seedpods.","The large edible seed of such a plant (for example, a broad bean, navy bean, or garbanzo bean)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hit with a projectile, especially a deliberately aimed blow to the head."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bean"},{"term":"hummus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Levantine Arab dip made of chickpea paste with various additions, such as olive oil, fresh garlic, lemon juice, and tahini, often eaten with pitta bread, or as a meze."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hummus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Phaseolus vulgaris","blocks":[{"text":"Phaseolus vulgaris, the common bean, is a herbaceous annual plant. Its botanical classification, along with other Phaseolus species, is as a member of the legume family, Fabaceae. It forms a green-leaved vine which produces beans inside of pods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Snijboon_peulen_Phaseolus_vulgaris.jpg/330px-Snijboon_peulen_Phaseolus_vulgaris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phaseolus_vulgaris","wikidata":"Q42339"},{"title":"Bean","blocks":[{"text":"A bean is the seed of plants in many genera of the legume family (Fabaceae) used as a vegetable for human consumption or animal feed. The seeds are sold fresh or preserved through drying (a pulse). Beans have been cultivated since the seventh millennium BCE in Thailand, and since the second millennium BCE in Europe and in Peru. Most beans, with the exception of peas, are summer crops. As legumes, the plants fix nitrogen and form seeds with a high protein content. They are produced on a scale of millions of tons annually in many countries, with India as the largest producer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/French_beans_J1.JPG/330px-French_beans_J1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bean","wikidata":"Q379813"},{"title":"Hummus","blocks":[{"text":"Hummus is a Levantine dip, spread, or savory dish made from cooked, mashed chickpeas blended with tahini, lemon juice, and garlic. The standard garnish includes olive oil, a few whole chickpeas, parsley, and paprika."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Lebanese_style_hummus.jpg/330px-Lebanese_style_hummus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hummus","wikidata":"Q241987"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White",